\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Afloat Vs Yen In Thin Pre-Holiday Trade \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2003\par 07:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar held steady against the yen in Asia Friday, as temporary position adjustments amid sluggish pre-holiday trade helped it enjoy continued respite from recent weakness. \par \par \uc2  "Looking at the big picture, the trend toward a weaker dollar probably hasn't changed," said Minoru Shioiri, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Mitsubishi Securities. \par \par \uc2  "But right now, people are taking a breather to contemplate if it's safe to keep selling blindly," especially before the long weekend. \par \par \uc2  U.S. markets will be closed Monday in observance of Memorial Day, while U.K. traders will have the same day off for a Bank Holiday. Activity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets usually tapers off ahead of holidays at major trading centers such as New York or London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also remained well-supported thanks to the "massive" yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities that rescued it from two-year lows earlier in the week, said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  Umemoto estimates the Bank of Japan has dumped at least Y4 trillion into the market at the behest of the Finance Ministry to keep the dollar above Y115, a level it nearly broke Monday. \par \par \uc2  "They absorbed so many dollars that the supply-demand dynamic is going to be changed for a while," he said. \par \par \uc2  The question is, however, where the dollar will head after it finishes its brief correction, Tokyo traders said. \par \par \uc2  For clues, players will look for any signs of change in euro-zone officials' relative indifference to the euro's recent rise, as well as factors which will likely sway the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it prepares for its policy board meeting next month, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.36, above Y117.22 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y117.57 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1675, lower than $1.1699 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.1650 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y137.02, down from Y137.14 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y136.97 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6326, down from $1.6352 in New York and lower than $1.6355 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders said they expect few implications for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to come out of the meeting between Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi and U.S. President George W. Bush in Texas later Friday. \par \par \uc2  The two leaders are likely to avoid the sensitive topic of exchange rates, as it would only highlight a growing rift over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of the two countries. \par \par \uc2  Recent comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow have suggested that he is abandoning Washington's long-standing "strong-dollar" policy. Snow has said that the dollar's recent slide has been a "really fairly modest realignment" and that a weaker dollar would help U.S. exports. \par \par \uc2  But even if the U.S. secretly wants \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if they don't say so there's likely to be little effect on the market, Mitsubishi's Shioiri said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets under the premise of curbing excessive volatility, so that it can keep the yen from rising too far against the dollar. Tokyo maintains that current economic fundamentals don't warrant a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said Friday morning large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves "affect" Japan firms, underscoring the market's view that the ministry has staunchly been defending the Y115-level, which is a break-even point for many of Japan's manufacturers. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par    -Edited by Alastair Gale and Bennett Richardson\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated\par hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030523dz5n000as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
