\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady above recent lows, euro eyes ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2003\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  By Charlotte Cooper LONDON, May 22 (Reuters) - The dollar held steady above recent lows on the yen and euro on Thursday, aided by modest optimism from the U.S. Federal Reserve, suspicion of Japanese yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and jitters over euro zone rates. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its regular mid-month policy meeting on Thursday and while no interest rate decision is expected, traders said there was some last-minute nervousness in the market it could cut rates. \par \par \uc2  Caution over possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also kept speculators from selling dollars for yen, keeping the greenback confined within a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "A marginal risk of (an ECB) rate cut may be holding the euro back today but I doubt it's going to happen," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "But more likely it's just dollar short covering as there hasn't been any turnaround in dollar sentiment, although (Federa Reserve chief Alan) Greenspan's comments yesterday may have given it a little bit of support." \par \par \uc2  By 0800 GMT, the euro was at $1.1650, a fraction up from its New York close but one cent below Wednesday's four-year peak at $1.1745, just a whisker off its 1999 launch rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was slightly firmer at 117.60 yen after hitting a two-week high in Asian trade and extending its recovery from Monday's two-year low of 115.10. \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady at 137.00 yen having hit a record high of 137.40 yen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  POLICYMAKERS IN FOCUS Analysts doubted the ECB would cut interest rates, now at 2.50 percent, on Thursday but some were forecasting a reduction at its June meeting after recent poor German growth data. \par \par \uc2  German regional inflation data is due at 0900 GMT, starting with the state of Hesse and followed by the other regions on Friday, with some analysts looking for inflation to edge down. \par \par \uc2  Finland's representative at the ECB said the strong euro was hitting French German and Finnish exports. \par \par \uc2  Matti Louekoski, deputising for Finnish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Matti Vanhala, told reporters: "(The euro) means problems because of our big dependence on exports." \par \par \uc2  In Asia, dealers suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York trade on Wednesday to squash any signs of gains in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some said it may have stepped in on Thursday too. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities are worried about the effect of a strong yen on exports and are widely seen as wanting to prevent the dollar from dropping through 115. \par \par \uc2  "Not many want to try an attack under 117.50 since that would be the same as challenging the authorities," said a trader at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said the yen's fall against the dollar from the previous day was a "natural correction" of an earlier move and declined to comment on whether authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In testimony before the U.S. Congress on Wednesday Greenspan gave few clues on monetary policy but called deflation a "minor threat" and held out hopes the U.S. economy would pick up. \par \par \uc2  Traders said expectations for a rate cut prior to the next Fed policy meeting had eased after Greenspan's comments. \par \par \uc2  "But the market is still anticipating a credit easing at the meeting," said a spot trader at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030523dz5m00g3n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
