\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Dn Late On Wage Cuts Call, Broader USD Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2003\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was weaker late Thursday as the specter of higher unemployment and proposed wage cuts hurt sentiment toward the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A broad U.S. dollar rise against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid continued concerns that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also contributed to the local dollar's falls, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  At 0810 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7260, compared with S$1.7247 late Wednesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7240 and S$1.7290 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.7270 early in Asia after recouping some losses against its Asian counterparts overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar extended its gains against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as market sentiment toward the local dollar was soured by the prospects of wage cuts, prolonged salary freezes and higher unemployment. \par \par \uc2  The National Wages Council, which advises the Singapore government on wage policies, said Wednesday that companies hurt by the SARS outbreak should cut wages to prevent job losses. For companies less affected by SARS but facing general business difficulties, the NWC recommended a wage freeze. \par \par \uc2  The government said Thursday it accepted the NWC recommendations, which aren't binding but are generally followed. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar also found strong support on speculation the Bank of Japan had sold yen to stem the recent slide of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the Asian session, the U.S. dollar was trading at Y117.68 against the yen, compared with its earlier low of Y117.44. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said, with the Singapore dollar currently considered to be somewhere near the midpoint of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band, they expected direct trading interest in the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair to be thin. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to trade between S$1.7240 and S$1.7330 overnight. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly lower as they tracked the overnight falls in short-dated U.S. Treasurys, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan to Congress overnight had generally reduced expectations of any immediate cut in U.S. rates, thus sparking modest unwinding of bonds almost across the curve, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the end of Thursday's session, the yield on two-year bonds was unchanged at 0.71%, while the yield on five-year bonds gained three basis points to 1.31%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds also rose three basis points to 1.65% and the yield on 10-year bonds was five basis points higher at 1.85%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended three basis points higher at 2.24%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, offers were also mostly higher as\par they tracked local bond yields. The two-year swap offer was one basis\par point higher at 0.89% while the five-year offer gained three basis\par points to 1.45%. The 10-year offer rose four basis points to 2.15%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 126 basis points\par from 124 basis points late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were steady as liquidity remained\par sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Thursday     Late Wednesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.5000% 0.5625%   0.4375% 0.5625%\par 3-Month           0.5000% 0.6250%   0.5000% 0.6250%\par 1-Year            0.5625% 0.6875%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Barry Deely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030522dz5m000im\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
