\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slides as market on alert for BOJ selling. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Javier David \par \uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2003\par 18:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 21 (Reuters) - The yen fell to its weakest level on record against the euro and slid against the dollar on Wednesday as traders were on guard that Japan may sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it from inflicting further damage on the economy. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan offering a balanced assessment of the U.S. economy's challenges, traders kept the dollar hemmed in tight ranges. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi warned against the yen's strengthening trend, saying officials were on alert for excessive moves. "We will act as necessary, when needed," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to prevent a muscular yen from undermining the country's export sector, its sole source of economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Attempting to fight the dollar's seemingly inexorable decline, they have used Japanese financial institutions to sell yen aggressively on their behalf - confounding many dealers in the process and keeping the market on its toes. \par \par \uc2  "Certainly the BoJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has been continuing their campaign of covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Woolfolk, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of New York. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary officials have "a clear policy mandate internally to prevent the yen from strengthening on a trade-weighted basis," he added. "While a considerable amount of Japanese exports head to the U.S.... the euro zone is certainly a large export destination for Japan and is likely to grow larger." \par \par \uc2  The dollar bought 117.20 yen  in afternoon U.S. trading, up 0.50 percent from its previous U.S. close and more than two full units above Monday's two-year low at 115.03 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded near 137.20 yen , up 0.35 percent on the day, off its highs but still at its highest since the euro began trading against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, 1999. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking drove the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower against the dollar from $1.1744 , a level fractionally below its January 1999 launch rate. In midday trading, it hovered just above $1.17, unchanged on the day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hunkered at a 4-1/2 year low against the Swiss franc, trading around 1.29 francs . \par \par \uc2  GREENSPAN CAUTIOUS BUT REASSURING \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said it was unclear whether the U.S. economy was at the "fulcrum" of a significant recovery. Testifying before the Joint Economic Committee of Congress, he said the potential danger posed by broadly falling prices was small but credible. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were briefly unsettled by Greenspan's comment that interest rates could be reduced further - extending the dollar's yield gap versus the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . By and large, however, the market was relieved by his general lack of concern over deflation. \par \par \uc2  "I actually think that he is maintaining his glass half full outlook, which to me is consistent with keeping rates on hold at the next meeting," said Lara Rhame, senior economist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York. \par \par \uc2  "At least it is consistent with Greenspan's sense that the Fed needs proof beyond reasonable doubt there are other problems in the U.S. economy beyond concerns revolving around the war" in Iraq, she added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1619GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par calculated from the levels at 5:30 p.m. (21:30 GMT) in the\par previous New York session.\par                       Last  US Close    %      YTD     2002\par                              20 May.  Change %Change    Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.1717   1.1714   +0.03  +11.63   1.0496\par Dlr/yen              117.15   116.60   +0.47   -1.34   118.74\par Euro/yen             137.20   136.62   +0.42  +10.05   124.67\par Dlr/swiss            1.2901   1.2906   -0.04   -6.60   1.3812\par Stg/dlr              1.6405   1.6406   -0.01   +1.83   1.6110\par Dlr/cad              1.3483   1.3471   +0.09  -14.24   1.5722\par Aus/dlr              0.6569   0.6583   -0.21  +17.12   0.5609\par Euro/swiss           1.5118   1.5119   -0.01   +4.29   1.4496\par Euro/stg             0.7138   0.7138   +0.00   +9.61   0.6512\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par  European markets......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030521dz5l00uk8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
