\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Holds Most Gains Vs Yen After BOJ Eases \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2003\par 07:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar slightly pared some of its Y2 overnight rise against the yen, but got some help in staying above Y117 support in Asia Tuesday from the Bank of Japan's decision to ease policy. \par \par \uc2  Citing what it called "unstable" stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and greater uncertainty about the economy's future, the BOJ's policy board voted to increase its liquidity target, measured by its account balance, to a range of Y27 trillion to Y30 trillion. Its previous target range had been Y22 trillion to Y27 trillion. \par \par \uc2  The dollar spent the morning session in a tight range of Y117.01-Y117.21. Most traders hesitated to test the downside after what most believe was a massive wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, which lifted the dollar off its Monday low of Y115.10. \par \par \uc2  The greenback initially ticked up within that small daily range after the BOJ's decision was announced, but dropped back almost immediately toward the lower end as U.S. funds sold into the rise. \par \par \uc2  The recent yen strength against the dollar "is the main concern of the BOJ," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. \par \par \uc2  But the easing alone won't be enough to keep the yen down for long, some traders and strategists said. \par \par \uc2  While the BOJ's easing "is good for weakening the yen, it doesn't promise a stronger dollar," said Tomoko Fujii, head of economic and market analysis at Nikko Citigroup. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.10, below Y117.34 in New York, but significantly above Y115.24 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1663, higher than $1.1658 in New York, but below $1.1688 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y136.57, compared with Y136.79 in New York and Y134.73 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6326, compared with $1.6325 in New York and $1.6288 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Corrected May 20, 2003 01:59ET (05:59GMT) \par \par \uc2  While the BOJ's easing "is good for weakening the yen, it doesn't promise a stronger dollar," said Tomoko Fujii, head of economic and market analysis at Nikko Citigroup. \par \par \uc2  (The effect on the dollar was misstated in an item that ran around 0543 GMT.) \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's move followed the government's weekend announcement that it plans to bailout Japan's fifth-largest bank, Resona Holdings Inc. That news led to stock and credit market weakness Monday. \par \par \uc2  Therefore, Tuesday's easing "was a kind of pre-emptive action in order to stabilize the financial market," said Satoru Ogasawara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston. "It was kind of a prudent policy, not a real monetary policy, and as such it won't have much impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said at a post-meeting press conference that all board members remain committed to ensuring stability in the financial markets. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is stronger against the dollar, but it hasn't risen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Fukui said, adding that the BOJ will keep a close watch on the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on the overall economy. \par \par \uc2  Although Japan's Finance Ministry, not the BOJ, sets \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, his remarks underscored the extent to which Japanese authorities perceive the yen's rise against the dollar as a serious threat to Japan's stalled economy. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Tuesday the ministry is "watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and if there are unnatural moves, there is a need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." He added that such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aren't aimed at protecting specific levels. \par \par \uc2  "We will take action to make sure that there aren't big moves," Vice Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said Tuesday, although he wouldn't comment on whether the ministry was behind the dollar's overnight surge. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030520dz5k000an\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
