\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar off lows in Asia,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected. \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2003\par 01:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 16 (Reuters) - The dollar was trading well above the two-year lows against the yen that it hit during U.S. trade in early dealings in Asia on Friday after suspected Japanese yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a Group of Seven meeting. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to as low as 115.30 yen , its lowest level since February 2001 on Thursday, on the perception that America's nonchalance over its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall could slow Japan's attempts to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help exports. \par \par \uc2  In recent days, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow has been critical of using \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fine-tune economic growth, all the while demonstrating little concern over the dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Especially when a weak dollar has been helping U.S. equity and Treasury markets, it's hard to think the U.S. authorities will loudly support strong dollar policy now," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Still, traders in London and New York said they believed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars on Thursday, bringing back the dollar to the 116.50 yen level. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent speculative moves. \par \par \uc2  Dealers will be watching how Snow and Shiokawa deal with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue at Group of Seven finance ministers meeting in France this weekend. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar stood at 116.44/49 yen  at 2306 GMT, little changed from the\par late U.S. level of 116.40/50 The euro stood at $1.1381/86       ,\par slightly up from $1.1372/78.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par German Finance Minister Hans Eichel said on Thursday the strong euro,\par which hit a four-year high against the dollar earlier this week, was\par creating scope for the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan will release first quarter gross domestic data at 2350 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030516dz5f0009k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
