\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ seen in surprise  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  ahead of G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2003\par 16:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 15 (Reuters) - Traders in London and New York said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to sell yen for dollars on Thursday, catching the markets unawares ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities declined to comment, but traders said a spike in the dollar of more than half a yen from two-year lows of 115.33 at the crossover hour between London and New York trading had all the hallmarks of covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The feeling is that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Banks which are buying dollars are the names associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a London-based trader. \par \par \uc2  "I guess they are using night desks in Tokyo." \par \par \uc2  Analysts had speculated that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts through the Bank of Japan, would be reluctant to incur the wrath of U.S. authorities so shortly before a meeting of finance ministers of top rich nations in Deauville, France on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow told Reuters in an interview earlier this week that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not well calculated to breed long-run domestic prosperity". \par \par \uc2  Snow holds a separate meeting with Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa at 1400 GMT on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. is against large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So what the Japanese have tended to do is to come in from time to time," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  Japan has failed to find support from U.S. or euro zone monetary authorities in its bid to cap the export-harming strength of the yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. has said it wants markets to determine the dollar's value and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the euro's current strength was no cause for concern. The euro hit record highs against the yen this week. \par \par \uc2  Japan has previously waited until G7 meetings were out of the way before carrying out solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Ahead of the last G7 meeting in February, the Japanese didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all ahead of the meeting but after the meeting they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the next seven business days," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  Recent data showed Japanese authorities spent 2.38 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from January to March, buying dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Yet with the G7 meeting still to come, traders in Tokyo said Japan was seen selling the yen on Tuesday, and London traders said Thursday's sharp move looked like a repeat action. \par \par \uc2  "Was it the BOJ? - Well, it certainly felt like it," said one trader. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030515dz5f00s8t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
