\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Vols Higher On Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2003\par 17:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Volatilities implied by one-month euro/dollar and dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options were mixed Thursday in New York, as the dollar shored up its gains against the euro and likely covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped halt the dollar's slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts had previously speculated that the MOF might be hesitant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the U.S.'s apparent opposition to efforts to slow the yen's rise at the dollar's expense, particularly ahead of this weekend's meeting of Group of Eight finance ministers in Deauville, France. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, traders said Japanese banks were buying the dollar as it hit its lowest levels. \par \par \uc2  Market professionals, however, questioned the effectiveness of such a unilateral move by BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "The current tone suggests that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may help but I'm just not sure about how long it's going to last," said David Mozina, director of global fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Bank of America Securities in New York. "The MOF can try to defend some line (in the sand), but for only so long." \par \par \uc2  U.S. economic data released Thursday morning ahead of the Philadelphia Fed Index this afternoon indicated continuing positive and negative aspects of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  While the number of U.S. workers filing first-time applications for unemployment benefits dropped last week for a third consecutive week, U.S. wholesale prices registered their biggest decline in at least 56 years in April, highlighting the Federal Reserve's worry that the economy faces a deflation risk. \par \par \uc2  Around 11:10 a.m. EDT (1510 GMT) Thursday, the dollar was trading at Y115.90, down from Y116.19 late Wednesday in New York but significantly above its session lows of Y115.35. The euro was trading at $1.1462, down from $1.1503 late Wednesday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at $1.3134, down from CHF1.3145 late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6233, up from $1.6175. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options implied volatility of 10.50%-10.70%, up from 9.90%-10.20% earlier in Tokyo. One-month euro/dollar option volatilities were at 10.40%-10.70%, down from 10.60%-10.75%, earlier in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  One-month risk-reversals on dollar/yen favor dollar puts at -1.80% to -1.50%. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  Euro calls are favored against the dollar by 0.50%-0.80%. \par \par \uc2  Volatility measures the expected range in the value of an asset over the period of the contract. Volatilities on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options gauge the anticipated moves in the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a higher volatility implying a wider trading range. \par \par \uc2  -By Michael Deibert, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2248; michael.deibert@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 44427 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030515dz5f00137\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
