\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Slips Vs Yen; Japan MOF Fears Steady Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Soble \par \uc2 847 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2003\par 07:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The resurgent yen extended its rebound against the euro in Asia trade Thursday but held steady against the dollar, sparking rumors Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were quietly supporting the greenback after its sharp fall overnight. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry ordered the Bank of Japan to dump billions of yen into the market overnight through Japanese commercial banks, many traders believe, as the dollar plunged to a fresh 10-month low around Y115.56. \par \par \uc2  Some speculated the MOF launched additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday to give the dollar some extra padding after it regained the psychologically important Y116 mark. But the greenback's overnight tumble had some analysts questioning Tokyo's ability to keep the U.S. unit afloat. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody thought Y116 was the MOF's formidable barrier, but they failed to hold it," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo. "Clearly their strategy is in question now." \par \par \uc2  The ministry has kept tight-lipped about its market moves in recent months, disclosing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  only days or weeks after the fact. So far this year, however, MOF officials have acknowledged spending nearly Y2.4 trillion to cap the surging yen. \par \par \uc2  The specter of MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept many dollar-yen players on the sidelines Thursday. But traders agreed the dollar would soon retest its overnight low, which lies just above its low for last year, hit July 16. \par \par \uc2  "There's a great big bull's-eye painted on Y115.50," a trader at a U.S. brokerage in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  A break of that level could spark an even sharper decline, pointing the dollar at least several yen lower in the short- to medium-term, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market would get very bearish very quickly," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, though, the yen's gains were limited primarily to the euro, which slid on continued profit-taking as players anticipated the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates at its June 5 meeting. \par \par \uc2  Tate predicted the euro would fall back to Y130.00 in the next two weeks - more than five yen off its highest-ever level of Y135.49, set Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.17, steady from Y116.19 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y116.68 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1440, lower than $1.1503 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1510 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y132.92, down from Y133.65 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y134.30 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6135, down from $1.6175 in New York but higher than $1.6083 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Technical charts were also working against the euro Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's drop against the yen this week has created a new downtrend line for the pair, and broader chart analysis suggests the single unit is likely to test underlying support around Y132.40 and could sink as low as its February peak of Y130.77 in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry - both verbal and real - is likely to slow the yen's rise against the dollar. But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts at JP Morgan said the greenback is failing to get support from another traditional ally - Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2  Japan-based investors haven't stopped buying U.S. assets - in fact, portfolio flows data for the period of May 6-9 showed a Y1.4 trillion outflow, the biggest since last April. The problem, the analysts said in a research note, is that investors are hedging their purchases, neutralizing the impact on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the pound shrugged off a report late Wednesday that Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown had ruled out U.K. adoption of the euro. \par \par \uc2  A Treasury spokesman denied the report by the British Broadcasting Corporation that Brown had concluded that the U.K. hadn't passed his five economic tests on whether the pound should be ditched in favor of the euro. \par \par \uc2  The denial helped mute sterling's reaction to the report, but analysts also noted that most market players already doubt the U.K. is ready to join the European common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The pound's biggest risk in the near term, JP Morgan's analysts said, is the Bank of England's inflation report due later Thursday, which could lead to "knee-jerk" movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030515dz5f000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
