\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-MOF denies weak yen policy,says G7 agrees on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2003\par 03:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 14 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied on Wednesday it was seeking a weaker yen, saying it only wanted to prevent excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and that its policy was in line with that of the United States and Group of Seven (G7). \par \par \uc2  "We don't have the intention of purposely taking the yen higher or lower. We want to prevent excessive moves," Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Worried that a stronger yen is hurting exporters, Japan spent 2.39 trillion yen to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first quarter and speculation is rife that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in recent days as the yen climbed to 10-month highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The G7 agrees that the market should reflect economic fundamentals, and that on the other hand, countries should cooperate if needed if there is volatility," Mizoguchi said. \par \par \uc2  Governments' policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been the focus of attention in the past few days as speculation has arisen that the U.S. has abandoned its strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterated his support for a strong dollar before a Congressional committee on Tuesday but he has alluded to the benefits of a weaker dollar on other occassions. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters, he expressed disapproval of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a way of helping an economy, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe should not blame a weaker dollar for their economic woes. \par \par \uc2  His comments sparked speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might find it more difficult diplomatically to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  When asked about Snow's remarks, Mizoguchi denied a rift between the U.S. and Japan. \par \par \uc2  "Our views haven't changed, and the views of the United States haven't changed either. We've been consistent, there's no difference of opinion," he said. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi is due to accompany Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa to Deauville, France, at the weekend to meet with finance ministers and officials from the rest of the G7 - the United States, Britain, Canada, France, Germany and Italy. \par \par \uc2  A senior MOF official said on Tuesday he saw little scope for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come up at the meeting or in bilateral talks with the United States tentatively set for Friday. \par \par \uc2  But with all three major economic blocs apparently keen to avoid further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, markets will be closely watching for comments from the G7 finance ministers. \par \par \uc2  Europe is also concerned that a recent surge in the euro, up more than 10 percent this year against the dollar to levels not seen since the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's birth in 1999, bodes ill for exports. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030514dz5e0038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
