\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen gains as market ponders Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Javier David \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2003\par 00:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 14 (Reuters) - The yen hit a 10-month high against the dollar and rose against the euro on Wednesday, after Japan denied it was seeking a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and declared its policy in line with its international counterparts. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  rejected suggestions it was seeking a weaker yen to stimulate its economy. Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, said Japan's only intent was to "prevent excessive moves." \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi sought to cast Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as in line with other members of the Group of Seven industrialized nations. But in an interview with Reuters released on Tuesday, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow strongly criticized Japanese government attempts to engineer a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With G7 finance ministers meeting in France this weekend, traders mulled the significance of Mizoguchi's remarks and pushed the yen broadly higher. \par \par \uc2  "In Japan the rhetoric has changed," said Steven Englander, chief North American \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in New York. "In the last few days the tone has been about preventing volatility rather than saying the yen is excessively strong." \par \par \uc2  Japan's actions, however, appear at odds with Snow's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the first quarter, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 2.39 trillion yen ($20.6 billion) in order to prevent a strong yen from dampening Tokyo's attempts to jump-start its economy. \par \par \uc2  Traders widely suspect monetary authorities have been trying to shore up the dollar versus the yen in recent days. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as far as 115.62 yen , its lowest since July 2002, before recovering to end the U.S. session at 116.25 yen. It was down 0.50 percent from its previous close, driven in part by heavy liquidation of euro/yen positions. \par \par \uc2  The euro settled at 133.56 yen , down 0.76 percent from its previous U.S. close and two units from its record high reached earlier this week. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also dipped against the dollar, ending the day below $1.15 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  POLICY BLITZ \par \par \uc2  Dollar weakness is becoming a big focus and has triggered a cacophony of official remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, French Finance Minister Francis Mer said the euro's rise against the dollar was "not very favorable in terms of (European) growth," and that there was room for movement on monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Mer's remarks come only a week after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expressed little concern about the strong euro. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the White House reaffirmed the "strong dollar" policy, backing up a similar flood of rhetoric from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow in recent days. \par \par \uc2  All of which puts Japan in the most difficult predicament, made clear by Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda warning that the government should act "decisively" against rapid moves in the market. \par \par \uc2  "This is where it becomes a challenge because all the officials can do is really slow the decline in dollar/yen, making you susceptible to violent moves. The important level in mind is 115.50 yen," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Merrill Lynch in New York. \par \par \uc2  In the United States, April retail sales fell 0.1 percent, with sales excluding autos sinking 0.9 percent, raising concerns that American consumers may be showing signs of fatigue. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030514dz5e0157j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
