\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar holds on to recent gains vs tired euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2003\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 14 (Reuters) - The dollar held onto the previous session's gains versus the euro on Wednesday after rising off recent four-year lows against a tired single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while fears of Japanese authorities buying greenbacks gave it added support. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar's rise was a dead cat bounce rather than a real rally, following its decline to multi-year lows versus major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently. Many saw the euro resuming its rise soon. \par \par \uc2  U.S. April retail sales data were due at 1230 GMT. Economists surveyed by Reuters expected sales to have risen 0.4 percent, or 0.1 percent excluding autos, in April, but some were positioned for worse, which might limit the dollar's reaction. \par \par \uc2  "The main question people are asking is where the next wave of dollar selling is going to coming from, so I think there has been a bit of a consolidation feel over the last couple of days," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "We're also looking at these retail sales numbers in the U.S. today. There's been a huge migration toward a pretty bad ex-autos number." \par \par \uc2  At 1145 GMT, the dollar was up a third of a percent against the euro from the previous session at $1.1487, after gaining more than a cent from the latest four-year lows of $1.1623 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar was flat on the day at 116.76, but up from recent 10-month lows around 116 yen. \par \par \uc2  SNOW, RATES AND BOJ IN FOCUS \par \par \uc2  Investors were also looking at fresh comments from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, who reaffirmed the Administration's "strong dollar" policy. \par \par \uc2  However, after sparking bouts of dollar-selling earlier this week by casting doubts over the policy, analysts say the "strong dollar" comments had a hollow ring. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody believes the strong dollar policy is a policy in anything but name," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  Markets were apprehensive about testing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after traders detected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling yen for dollars in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  "I certainly think it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is a factor on players' minds.... Clearly levels between 116 and 116.50/60 are the danger levels," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Ministry denied Tokyo was seeking a weaker yen to help exporters and said it only wanted to prevent excessive market moves. \par \par \uc2  Markets were nevertheless edgy after Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda issued a fresh warning the government should act "decisively" against rapid moves in the market. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said he did not see \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  being an issue in talks with U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow on the sidelines of a Group of Seven (G7) meeting this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also helped earlier by Tuesday's comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) Governing Council member Ernst Welteke, who said the bank could have room for interest rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  However, he was also quoted on Wednesday as saying monetary policy was helping rather than hindering the euro zone economy. \par \par \uc2  "The euro seems to have run out of steam. Welteke's comments yesterday...will temper further euro gains from here," said Halpenny. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030514dz5e00nrx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
