\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Settles Mixed, Drops Against Yen, Gains on Euro \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robert Flint and Michael Deibert \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2003\par 22:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -- The yen danced a wild jig around the dollar and euro Wednesday, surging at one point to a fresh ten-month peak against its U.S. rival as traders appeared to test the resolve of Japanese authorities to slow the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar seemed content to waltz sedately with the euro, closing a bit higher against the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with investors pausing to book profits on the euro's recent gains. \par \par \uc2  The yen's rapid rise was the focus of the New York session, raising the specter of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  using the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. Traders are convinced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly earlier this week and last week, channeling funds through Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  The wave of profit-taking that kept the dollar steady against the euro apparently originated in the euro/yen cross and ultimately placed pressure on the dollar/yen pair, analysts said. A growing sense that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates at its meeting on June 5 is reducing the euro's attraction. In recent weeks, the euro, supported by the ECB's benchmark rate being at 2.50%, has raced ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from countries that offer lower interest rates, such as the U.S. and Japan. \par \par \uc2  "People are becoming more and more convinced that the ECB is going to cut rates and that's taking some of the froth off the appreciation the euro," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Bank Julius Baer in New York. "We're playing more off what the ECB is going to be doing and less off the U.S. data." \par \par \uc2  Interest-rate considerations also are playing in favor of sterling, in addition to recent positive economic numbers out of the United Kingdom. Sterling advanced Wednesday both against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly the U.K. is moving toward the end of its cycle while the euro zone hasn't even begun," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Weaker-than-expected U.S. retail sales had only a minor effect on the dollar Wednesday, analysts noted. Sales fell by 0.1% in April, after a revised 2.3% gain in March, the Commerce Department said. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the dollar was trading at 116.19 yen, down from 116.60 yen late Tuesday in New York. The euro was trading at $1.1503, down slightly from $1.1513 late Tuesday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3145 francs, steady from 1.3140 francs late Tuesday. Sterling was at $1.6175, up from $1.6091. \par \par \uc2  The gains for the yen came after U.S Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterated Tuesday that governments ought not to try to influence \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Analysts wondered whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be hesitant to act given the U.S.'s apparent opposition to efforts to slow the yen's rise at the dollar's expense, particularly ahead of this weekend's meeting of Group of Eight finance ministers in Deauville, France. \par \par \uc2  "We feel there is far less likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hours before Snow and [Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro] Shiokawa meet face to face," said Tim Mazanec, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Investors Bank & Trust. \par \par \uc2  "We do, however expect some verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tonight, with Japanese officials reiterating that rapid moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not desirable," Mr. Mazanec added. \par \par \uc2  But earlier Wednesday, Mr. Shiokawa said that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be on the agenda when he holds talks with Mr. Snow Friday in France. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Flint and Michael Deibert, Dow Jones \par \par \uc2  Newswires, 201-938-4408; robert.flint@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  05-14-03 1655ET \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020030514dz5e006hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
