\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar off lows, market wary of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2003\par 01:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 14 (Reuters) - The dollar recovered slightly from its recent lows against the yen in early Asia on Wednesday as investors sensed that monetary authorities in Tokyo could step into the market at any time to try to weaken Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also underpinned by comments late on Tuesday by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow before a Congressional committee in which he reiterated his support for a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  He also said there was no conscious policy by the United States to move the value of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Snow has been in the market spotlight for the last few days, alluding to the benefits a weaker dollar on exports and casting doubt on the benefits of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Snow's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments knocked the dollar down as low as 116.36 yen  in late Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 116.77/78 yen  at 2335 GMT, up slightly from 116.58.66 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  "Market participants can't sell the dollar because it's believed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "Ahead of the Group of Seven meeting (starting Friday), market participants are nervously waiting to see what other comments government officials will make," Hanao said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was expected to take a breather after its recent rally on speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may cut interest rates soon. \par \par \uc2  ECB board member Ernst Welteke said on Tuesday the bank had room to lower interest rates if oil prices and the dollar stayed low for long enough. The euro stood at $1.1527/32  at 2335 GMT, little changed from its late U.S. level of $1.1531/37. \par \par \uc2  One factor restraining the dollar was the report showing U.S. trade deficit swelled in March to $43.5 billion, its second-highest level on record. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030513dz5d017tu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
