\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar repairs Snow damage with Japan's help. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2003\par 12:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fought back against the yen and the euro on Tuesday, aided by the Bank of Japan, after fresh comments from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow sent it reeling. There was no confirmation from Japanese authorities they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but traders in Tokyo said they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars for yen after the greenback was knocked a yen lower by Snow. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters conducted on Friday but embargoed until Tuesday, Snow attacked any efforts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe should not blame a weaker dollar for their economic woes. \par \par \uc2  This came on top of his comments over the weekend that a cheap dollar would help U.S. exports, which sent the dollar to a four-year low of $1.1623  against the euro on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Rhetoric like that suggests there is no major restriction coming from the U.S. for investors to sell the dollar. But the message from Japan is clear: they don't want to see the yen strengthening," said Osman Wahid, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  Snow speaks again at 2000 GMT on Tuesday, testifying before a House Financial Services Committee hearing on the state of the international financial system and IMF-related issues. \par \par \uc2  By 1000 GMT the dollar stood half a cent higher from Monday's New York close, at $1.1504 per euro, more than a cent above the Monday low. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was a quarter percent higher on the day versus the yen  at 117.11, having risen sharply from the Snow-induced lows around 116.37, the level at which traders said the BOJ had been seen starting its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the yen was a third of a percent up on the day at 134.81 . \par \par \uc2  GLOBAL COMPETITIVE DEVALUATION? \par \par \uc2  Snow told Reuters that devaluation strategies were not calculated to breed long-run domestic prosperity, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept to a minimum and relative values of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be determined through open exchange markets. \par \par \uc2  Japan, concerned that the yen's rise against the dollar could damage hopes for economic recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the first quarter of this year to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa and Snow, along with other G8 finance ministers, meet in France this weekend. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese and U.S. monetary officials have had a good relationship. Now they both want a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Has the relationship been strained? Maybe. It will be interesting to see what comes out of the summit," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say U.S. international trade data due later on Tuesday contains a potential dollar negative factor, with the figures expected to show the trade gap widened slightly in March to $40.75 billion from $40.32 billion in February. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the day is light on data except for the ZEW institute's expectations indicator for the German economy. The index, often an indicator for the Ifo German business index later in the month, edged up 0.3 points to 18.7 points in May, its fifth consecutive rise. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030513dz5d00kuk\par }\page 