\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Sinks Vs Rivals On US Snow's Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2003\par 07:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar sank against its major rivals in Asia Monday after weekend remarks by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow sent a clear signal to players to dump the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Providing dollar bears with a perfect excuse to get rid of the U.S. unit, Snow said Sunday that a weaker dollar could help U.S. exports, prompting a heavy wave of dollar sales across the board. \par \par \uc2  The speculator-led selling of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the euro to a fresh 52-month high of $1.1579 and dragged the dollar below the psychologically key Y117 level for the first time since last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "On the basis of these comments, we expect the dollar to remain weak against the euro," said Deutsche Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Marshall Gittler in a research report. \par \par \uc2  However, fears that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will put a floor under the sagging dollar will limit its downside against the yen, Gittler said. \par \par \uc2  Fanning those fears early in the session, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official warned traders not to push the yen higher. "We're continuing to watch markets closely and we will take the most appropriate measures for the situation," said Zembei Mizoguchi, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Finance Ministry followed through on its yen-selling threat as it quietly stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this morning via Japanese banks to buy dollars in the mid-Y116s to brake the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. The ministry was also widely rumored to have bought dollars for yen last Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  In another warning shot at yen bulls later in the session, Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda said the government stands ready to take firm steps to check the yen's appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "If there are extreme moves, we will take bold steps" to curb the yen's rise, Fukuda told a regular press conference. \par \par \uc2  Around 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.88, below Y117.23 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y117.34 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1560, higher than $1.1493 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.1517 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.07, up from Y134.73 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y135.17 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Despite its massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry still has a huge war chest it can use to cap the yen's resurgence, said Morgan Stanley's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Toru Umemoto in a research report. \par \par \uc2  Umemoto said the ministry can conduct as much as Y32.5 trillion of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the difference between the current ceiling on the issuance of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills and the outstanding amount of these \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills. \par \par \uc2  According to his estimates, the outstanding amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills is roughly Y46.5 trillion. At the same time, the current ceiling on total issued \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills was raised to Y79 trillion from this April in the initial budget for this fiscal year through next March. \par \par \uc2  When the finance ministry conducts yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills are issued to finance the yen to be sold. \par \par \uc2  Umemoto expects the dollar to trade sideways in a Y116-Y121 range for the next month, with the market's focus on possible MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japanese investors' capital outflows and global economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro surged to a fresh all-time high in Asia Monday, rising as high as Y135.49 on the coattails of the euro's rally against the dollar early in the session. \par \par \uc2  But Japanese exporters immediately sold euros for yen around that level to hedge against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, which helped to drag the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to the low Y135s. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6079, up from $1.6038 in New York and higher than $1.6025 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030512dz5c000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip