\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits 4-year high on Snow comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2003\par 01:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 12 (Reuters) - The euro hit another four-year high against the dollar on Monday after U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said a cheap U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help U.S. exports. \par \par \uc2  "When the dollar is at a lower level it helps exports, and I think exports are getting stronger as a result," Snow said on a U.S. television programme on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  On another programme, Snow said Washington was commited to a strong dollar but that its value would be set by markets. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that he mentioned the benefits of a weak dollar could be taken as a sign that he accepts weak dollar. His comments will set the tone of the market this week," said Shogo Nagaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Trust and Banking Corp in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been steadily weakening in recent weeks on doubts about the outlook for the U.S. economy and due to lower U.S. interest rates compared to those of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As of 2320 GMT, the euro was at $1.1572/77 , up about three quarters of a percent from about $1.1490 in late U.S. trade on Friday, and hitting its highest level since January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit a record high against the yen, touching 135.40/52 yen  from around 134.67 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's slide against the yen was curbed by wariness that Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The greenback slipped to 116.80/85 yen  by 2320 GMT, down from about 117.20 yen in U.S. trade, but still some way off its recent 10-month bottom of 116 yen hit last week. \par \par \uc2  Talk swirled late last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently but the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  "The data the government recently announced showed they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on many days early this year so I think they could be in the market any time," said Nagaya. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Japan said it sold the yen for dollars and euros on 17 days in the first quarter of 2003, starting from January 15 when the dollar fell below 118 yen in the run-up to the U.S.-led war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030511dz5b00v0p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
