\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro gyrates near new highs vs. key  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Javier David \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 18:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 9 (Reuters) - The euro orbited just below a four-year high against the dollar on Friday, tempered by modest profit-taking but underpinned by the yield advantage of European assets over U.S. investments. \par \par \uc2  After the euro hit its highest level since January 1999 against the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and surpassed its launching prices against both the yen and British pound, traders used gains in Wall Street stocks as an excuse to pare euro positions in early U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  However, most market participants say the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally is all but destined to continue, even as the euro zone's economies continue to falter. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hold interest rates steady on Thursday underscored the primary pillar of the euro's rally - the relatively higher returns investors receive holding European assets as opposed to lower-yielding U.S. financial instruments. \par \par \uc2  "The numbers out of Europe are pretty bad but we are not looking at growth differentials or prospects. We're basically looking at yield," said John McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Capital Markets in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the ECB didn't cut rates yesterday maintains a healthy yield spread to the dollar. That is the story, and the driving force behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves." \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded just below $1.15 against the dollar, off the day's lows near $1.1450  but below a new four-year high at $1.1535 reached in London trading. The euro is now about 2 cents from its launch price at $1.17. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded near unchanged against the Japanese yen at 134.64 , pulling off a record high at 135.30 yen. It slipped from a high of 71.94 pence against sterling  to stand around 71.60 pence. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, suspected yen-selling by Japan helped support the dollar against the yen. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 117.25 yen , up about 0.15 percent on the day and well above this week's 10-month low at 116.02 yen. \par \par \uc2  YIELD APPEAL \par \par \uc2  The ECB's decision to keep rates steady at 2.50 percent came after the U.S. Federal Reserve earlier this week highlighted the risk to the economy from falling inflation and hinted at its readiness to cut rates while holding rates steady at 1.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  ECB chief Wim Duisenberg said on Friday that the bank needed more evidence, notably on the impact of a rising euro on growth, before deciding whether it should cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone politicians are becoming restive about the euro's gains, underscoring the delicate line between an appropriately priced \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an overvalued one. French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin said it would be "worrying" if the euro reaches a level that hurts exports. \par \par \uc2  Daniel Katzive, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Connecticut, wrote in a research note to clients: "While we can't rule out an odd comment warning about euro strength from government officials, we do not expect the ECB to be an obstacle to further euro gains." \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the yen had strengthened too much but declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the yen's rise. Shiokawa's deputy, Zembei Mizoguchi, also declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900vy1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
