\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro holds at lofty peaks after breathtaking rally. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 9 (Reuters) - The euro held near four-year highs against the dollar and record peaks against the yen and the pound on Friday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep interest rates on hold gave new legs to its rally. \par \par \uc2  The euro - which has gained eight percent on the dollar and six percent on the yen in the past month - rose above $1.1530  in early trade, a level last seen just days after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was launched in January 1999. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It also pushed to record highs of 135.30 yen  and 71.94 British pence\par         before running out of steam in the European midsession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro's ability to extend gains overnight shows its uptrend is as\par strong as ever," said Ian Gunner, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Mellon\par Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "However, things seem to have settled down a bit now and after a very\par choppy few days traders are saying enough's enough."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With no major U.S. data due for release on Friday, Gunner said there\par may be a temptation to take profits on the euro's gains when New York\par opens for trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par YIELD APPEAL\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision on Thursday to leave\par euro zone interest rates unchanged was the catalyst for the euro's\par latest leg higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 2.50 percent, benchmark interest rates in the euro zone are twice\par that in the United States and compared with near-zero interest rates in\par Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ECB's no-change decision came after the U.S. Fed earlier this week\par highlighted the risk to the economy from falling inflation and hinted\par at its readiness to cut rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro's gains have been surprisingly rapid and come after dovish\par comments from the Fed and a tough stance from the ECB," said Shahab\par Jalinoos, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECB chief Wim Duisenberg said on Friday that the bank needed more\par evidence, notably on the impact of a rising euro on growth, before\par deciding whether it should cut interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Duisenberg said the euro, at its present level, was not yet hurting\par growth and the competitiveness of European firms was the same as the\par average of the past 30 years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MASSAGING THE YEN LOWER?\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro rose more than 2.5 percent from Thursday's lows against the\par yen, amid talk in the market of covert yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par Japanese authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This also lifted the dollar to 117.35 yen , up more than a yen from\par 10-month lows set in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen has risen four percent against the dollar in two weeks, raising\par concern its strength will make Japanese products more expensive abroad\par and dampen the country's exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I presume there was some form of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a trader in\par London, noting that Japanese authorities would be keen to prevent the\par dollar sliding through major technical support levels below 116.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the yen had\par strengthened too much but declined to comment on whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to stem the yen's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shiokawa's deputy, Zembei Mizoguchi, also declined to comment on\par whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the yen was also undermined by falling Japanese interest\par rates. The yield on 30-year Japanese government bonds fell below one\par percent to a record low 0.995 percent on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900nm1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
