\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro stays top-dog at $1.15, at 4-yr highs. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 12:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 9 (Reuters) - The euro powered to new four-year highs against the dollar and record highs against the yen and the pound on Friday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep interest rates on hold gave new legs to its rally. \par \par \uc2  The euro - which has gained eight percent on the dollar and six percent on the yen in the past month - rose above $1.1530 for the first time since January 1999, the month the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was launched. \par \par \uc2  It also hit a record high of 135.30 yen and 71.94 British pence before paring gains. \par \par \uc2  "The euro's gains have been surprisingly rapid and come after dovish comments from the Fed and a tough stance from the ECB," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  With no major U.S. economic data due on Friday, dealers said there was little reason to stand against the trend. \par \par \uc2  The ECB on Thursday left interest rates unchanged at 2.50 percent, leaving the relative yield attraction of euro zone deposits and fixed income investments intact. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's no-change decision came after the U.S. Fed earlier this week hinted at its readiness to cut rates, already at four-decade lows, citing the risk of falling inflation. Comments from ECB chief Wim Duisenberg that the current level of the euro was not excessive and that it would take longer than expected for inflation to fall below two percent gave more fodder for euro bulls. \par \par \uc2  MASSAGING THE YEN LOWER? \par \par \uc2  The euro rose more than 2.5 percent from Thursday's lows against the yen, amid talk in the market of covert yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  This also lifted the dollar to 117.35 yen , up more than a yen from 10-month lows set in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen four percent against the dollar in two weeks, raising concern its strength will make Japanese products more expensive abroad and dampen the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  "I presume there was some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader in London. \par \par \uc2  "There are some big levels Japan wants to protect on the (dollar/yen) downside so I would expect more of the same today." \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the yen had strengthened too much but declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's deputy, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, also declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but warned authorities would act if needed. \par \par \uc2  "As always, we will take action if necessary depending on market conditions," Mizoguchi told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite possible that the Japanese have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stephen Lewis, chief economist at Monument Derivatives. \par \par \uc2  "They do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in these markets without telling us." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar also drew some support due to falling Japanese interest rates. The yield on 30-year Japanese government bonds fell below one percent to a record low 0.995 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900k2f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
