\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits record high vs yen,4-year high vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 9 (Reuters) - The euro hit record highs against the yen and its best since January 1999 against the dollar on Friday as investors continued to flock to high yields after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep interest rates on hold. \par \par \uc2  The latest surge in the euro, which has climbed 10 percent against the dollar in six weeks, was also fuelled by ECB chief Wim Duisenberg's comment after Thursday's decision that it would take longer than expected for inflation to fall below two percent. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose more than 2.5 percent from Thursday's lows against the yen, amid talk in the market of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB's decision yesterday and Duisenberg's comments suggest the ECB might not be as eager to cut rates as the market supposed," said Stephen Lewis, chief economist at Monument Derivatives. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite possible that the Japanese have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  - they do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in these markets without telling us." \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose above 135.20 yen, beating its previous record high set on January 4, 1999, the euro's first day of trading, before retreating to 134.80 yen by 0720 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as $1.1535 , only two cents below its launch level against the dollar, before correcting to around $1.15. It also hit record highs against sterling for a second straight day, approaching 72 pence. \par \par \uc2  Global investors have been pouring funds into high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few weeks, and the benchmark euro zone rate of 2.50 percent is double the Federal Reserve's federal funds rate. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's no-change decision came after the U.S. Fed earlier this week hinted at its readiness to cut rates, already at four-decade lows, citing the risk of an unwanted fall in inflation. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, speaking in Washington late on Thursday, said a "wobbly" U.S. recovery was being restrained by weak economic performance in Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WORRY \par \par \uc2  Thanks to the euro's rise against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at 117.24 yen, well above the overnight 10-month low of 116 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen four percent against the dollar in two weeks, raising concern its strength will make Japanese products more expensive abroad and dampen the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was helped on Friday by talk of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities on Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  "I presume there was some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader in London. \par \par \uc2  "There are some big levels Japan wants to protect on the downside so I would expect more of the same today." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the yen has strengthened too much but declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's deputy, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, also declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but warned that it would act if needed. \par \par \uc2  "As always, we will take action if necessary depending on market conditions," Mizoguchi told reporters on his way to work. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar also drew some support due to falling Japanese interest rates. The yield on 30-year Japanese government bonds fell below one percent to a record low 0.995 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900fg1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
