\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro holds near multi-year highs after ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 03:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 9 (Reuters) - The euro held on to multi-year highs on Friday morning after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to keep interest rates at current levels, leaving intact the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attraction as a yield earner. \par \par \uc2  The latest rally was also fueled by ECB chief Wim Duisenberg's comment that there was nothing excessive about the current level of the euro. \par \par \uc2  Junya Tanase, global markets officer at J.P. Morgan Chase, said: "Now that the Fed is on an easing bias and the ECB has kept its rate steady (at 2.50 percent), I think the market is expecting a further widening of the yield gap between the dollar and the euro." \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as $1.1535 - a fresh four-year high - in early Asian trading before standing at $1.1525/30 . Dealers said the next target was $1.16. \par \par \uc2  The euro opened at $1.1745 at its launch in January 1999, and is expected to inch up towards that level. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a high of 135.11 yen  in early trading, just shy of a record high of 135.13 yen hit shortly after its launch. \par \par \uc2  "The trend of strong euro and weak dollar looks set to continue," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at the Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Thanks to the euro's rise against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at 117.15/16 yen , well above the overnight 10-month low of 116 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen about four percent against the dollar in two weeks, raising concern that its strength will make Japanese products more expensive abroad and dampen the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also helped by concerns about possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the yen has strengthened too much but declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A rumour circulated among market participants that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight when the yen appreciated to 116 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's deputy, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, also declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he warned that it would act if needed. \par \par \uc2  "As always, we will take action if necessary depending on market conditions," Mizoguchi told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Thursday showed Japanese authorities spent 2.38 trillion yen ($20.33 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the January-March quarter, buying dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Apart from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns, dealers said the dollar drew some downside support as Japanese investors are expected to keep snapping up foreign bonds amid the yen's rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors are desperate for higher-yielding assets as Japan's long-term interest rates have kept falling to record low levels. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the key 20-year Japanese government bond (JGB) fell to a record low of 0.890 percent, and the benchmark 10-year bond yield fell to a new low of 0.580 percent. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry data for capital flows in the week ended last Friday showed Japanese investors bought a net 425.3 billion yen of foreign bonds after buying 527 billion yen the previous week. ($1=117.09 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz590033a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
