\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro retests 4-yr high vs dollar as ECB stands pat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2003\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 8 (Reuters) - The euro jumped half a cent to retest four-year peaks on the dollar on Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates steady and the yen nervously held recent gains after officials warned about its rise. \par \par \uc2  Most economists had expected the ECB to keep rates steady but markets grew nervous about a possible cut ahead of the decision. Holding rates at 2.5 percent will keep in tact the euro zone's attractive yield advantage over the U.S. \par \par \uc2  "The decision is helping the euro," said Peter Fontaine, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at KBC in Brussels. \par \par \uc2  "The interest rate support is very important and the ECB is not taking it away. Next month is the last time the ECB can cut before a revolution breaks out in Europe because of the strong euro." \par \par \uc2  The euro hit the day's highs of $1.1452 by 1210 GMT, almost matching Tuesday's four-year high of $1.1453. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell more than 1.5 percent against the yen on Wednesday but rebounded half a percent to 132.80 yen on Thursday, compared with Tuesday's four-year highs of 134.48. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has leapt by nine percent against the dollar in the past six weeks, as investors flocked to higher-yielding assets. The ECB's benchmark rate of 2.50 percent compares with the U.S. federal funds rate of 1.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Sterling jumped to the day's highs against the dollar and the euro after the Bank of England left interest rates unchanged at 3.75 percent, keeping sterling's yield premium intact. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar fell to 4-1/2-year lows versus the Swiss franc below 1.3200. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  NERVES \par \par \uc2  The yen's recent bounce has also raised speculation Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to sell their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to protect their own export markets. A slew of warnings from Japanese officials on Thursday heightened this fear and speculation abounded in the market that Japanese authorities were trying curb yen gains by stealth. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said officials were watching moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates during European hours and were staying alert to rapid moves and would be watching the outcome of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy. \par \par \uc2  However, this was the latest and most specific in a string of similar comments by Finance Ministry officials but did little to undermine the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at the day's lows around 116.09 yen, compared with 10-month lows at 116.02 yen set in New York trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The yen has passed trigger levels you normally see (around \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ).... Against this background I would say they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Klawitter, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist West LB. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Thursday showed Japanese authorities spent 2.38 trillion yen ($20.44 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the January-March quarter, buying the dollar and euro. \par \par \uc2  During the past three years, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  every time the dollar fell towards 115 yen. In the January-March quarter, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  well before the dollar closed in on 115 yen, acting when it fell to around 117. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030508dz5800o30\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
