\par\par \b \uc2  Yen pauses after recent leap, euro soft before ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2003\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 8 (Reuters) - The yen paused for breath in early European trade on Thursday with dealers nervous of extending the previous day's stunning gains after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it was that ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter rapid market moves. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in the past one to two weeks had been rapid and officials would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they saw the need. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi's comments helped the dollar claw back to 116.45 yen , up almost half a yen from the previous session's 10-month low. \par \par \uc2  Euro traded with a softer bias at 131.90 yen  having fallen more than 1.5 percent on Wednesday in an abrupt reversal from this week's four-year high. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also weaker at $1.1330 , more than a cent below this week's four-year peak, as nervousness ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate decision at 1145 GMT encouraged dealers to take profits. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England is due to conclude a policy meeting at 1100 GMT with the market evenly split on whether the bank will leave British interest rates unchanged at 3.75 percent or cut by a quarter-point. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030508dz5800dqp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
