\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Pares Overnight Losses Vs Yen; ECB Awaited \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2003\par 07:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar regained some ground on the yen Thursday and also nudged higher against the euro ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting later this session. \par \par \uc2  Market consensus is that the ECB will hold interest rates steady, but market participants continued to use the meeting as an excuse to protectively take profits on the euro after its rise to four-year highs against the dollar and yen this month. \par \par \uc2  In Asian trading, most of the euro profit-taking centered on the yen, and that helped lift the dollar in crosstrading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also got a lift on warnings from Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. Both the ministry official who briefed on foreign reserves data, as well as Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, threatened Japan would act as needed after the dollar dropped to a 10-month low of Y116.07 overnight. \par \par \uc2  But some market participants were skeptical that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  under present market conditions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data for 2003 released earlier Thursday showed that yen-selling was most effective when the market was significantly dollar-short, and "the market's not particularly short at the moment - we don't seem to have that large overhang yet," said J.P. Morgan strategist James Malcolm. \par \par \uc2  But positions notwithstanding, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "risks get higher the lower down we go," he added. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.67, above Y116.40 late Wednesday in New York but more than a full yen below Y117.69 in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1317, below $1.1358 Wednesday in New York and $1.1412 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y132.04, compared with Y132.21 in New York and Y134.29 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5953, compared with $1.5962 in New York and $1.6130 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders said that as long as market fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keep the dollar above Y116, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to refrain from actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But authorities "would step in if the dollar went below Y116," and risked triggering stops down to Y115.50, said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The ministry data released Thursday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent Y2.387 trillion in 24 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  between January and March in an effort to cap the yen's rise against the dollar and the euro. Japanese financial authorities fear a strong yen would make Japanese exports less competitive in overseas markets and add to deflationary pressure at home. \par \par \uc2  A rising yen also threatens Japan's beleaguered life insurance companies. Not only does it wipe out profits on the overseas assets they left unhedged, but it risks canceling gains on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked speculative bets some of the larger companies made. Some market estimates say $5 billion-$10 billion could be wiped out for every yen the dollar drops between Y110 and Y115. \par \par \uc2  The instruments pay a market rate, such as the 10-year JGB yield plus a spread as long as the dollar doesn't hit any knockout levels. But if the knockout is hit, the insurers get their principle back but earn no return at all. \par \par \uc2  "The perception of systemic risk for the financial sector would get much larger if those were to be knocked out," said J.P. Morgan's Malcolm. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by John Gibson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030508dz58000bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
