\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro slips ahead of ECB rate decision. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Javier David \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2003\par 22:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 7 (Reuters) - The euro fell against the dollar and yen on Wednesday, hurt by speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may reduce interest rates and erode the yield advantage enjoyed by the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a whipsaw session that saw the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed more than a cent from Tuesday's 4-year low as traders booked profits, markets began to look ahead to the ECB's interest rate policy meeting scheduled for Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the ECB to keep benchmark rates steady at 2.25 percent, as monetary policymakers have in recent days telegraphed those intentions to the market. \par \par \uc2  But in the wake of Tuesday's decision by the Federal Reserve to hold U.S. rates steady, while indicating the economy still faced further weakness and falling prices, market observers say the ECB can ill afford to hold off on cutting much longer, as Europe's fundamentals deteriorate by the day. \par \par \uc2  "There is some dialogue occurring in the market that the ones that have the opportunity to stimulate their economies are the Europeans, and that would be with a rate cut," said Michael McGuinness, head of North American sales at American Express Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Germany - the euro zone's largest economy - announced that the jobless rate hit a five-year high. \par \par \uc2  Though a rate cut could stimulate the economy, it would narrow the yield differential that has allowed the euro to rally broadly, McGuinness added. "That's why we're off by more than a cent," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell as far as $1.1331 against the dollar, recovering slightly to trade near $1.1370 in late U.S. dealings. It was off by more than 0.60 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro also gave up Tuesday's four-year low against the yen, falling 1.70 percent from its prior U.S close to stand near 132.23 yen. \par \par \uc2  Broad dollar weakness converged with heavy euro/yen liquidation, traders said, dragging the dollar to its lowest in 10 months against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In late U.S. trading, the dollar bought 116.30 yen, off more than 1 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the yen's sharp rise against most major units heightened the risk that Japan could sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to weaken it. \par \par \uc2  "The next major level to look out for is 115.80 and I think that as we move toward that level the risk of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could become more acute," said Alex Beuzelin, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst at Ruesch International in Washington, D.C. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR REBOUNDS ON EURO \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the Fed signaled they may reduce U.S. rates from their current 1.25 percent. Meanwhile, European interest rates are at 2.50 percent, leading investors to shift money into euro zone assets and out of the United States. \par \par \uc2  However, the euro's nearly 8 percent surge against the dollar in the last month is raising concerns it has moved too far too fast. Several German manufacturers have complained that the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hurt their competitiveness in global markets. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030507dz57013cu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
