\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar off lows as U.S. signals concern. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2003\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - A show of support by Washington lifted the dollar from its latest nadir against the euro and the yen on Wednesday, but the rebound was far from confident after the Federal Reserve sowed more doubt over its outlook. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's public backing for a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the dollar off its lows, which came after the Fed left interest rates unchanged but warned the economy remained at risk of further weakness. \par \par \uc2  A further fall in rates would bode ill for the dollar, which has already been losing funds to the higher-yielding euro. \par \par \uc2  "We think a strong dollar is in the U.S. interest," Snow said in an interview on CNBC television. "The way to have a strong dollar and a dollar that is widely accepted as a good medium of exchange is to work on the fundamentals of the economy." \par \par \uc2  Toshiyuki Suzuki, economist at UFJ Bank in New York, said Snow's comment showed the United States is worried that a weaker dollar could lead to a fund drain away from U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  "For capital-import oriented United States, it's not good at all if the market holds view that the dollar would keep falling," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers even suspected that Snow's remarks were aimed at attracting offshore investors to the U.S. government's record $58 billion Treasury refunding this week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 117.65/68 yen at 0512 GMT, up from around 117.50 in late New York, and a one-month low around 117.29 yen hit in post-Asian trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1413/16 down from around $1.1440 in late U.S. business and a fresh four-year high of $1.1455. \par \par \uc2  The euro was further bolstered by remarks from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member Ernst Welteke on Tuesday that the rising euro was not holding back growth in Europe and is no cause for concern. \par \par \uc2  "I think the euro's firmness will continue for some time, and the (Fed) statement last night could add momentum," said Masamichi Koike, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trading group at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  Koike and other dealers said they expected the euro to test the $1.15 barrier soon. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  FEAR \par \par \uc2  One of the few things supporting the dollar is rising nerves about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which conducted "stealthy" yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the mid-117 yen level in January. \par \par \uc2  "We're at a level where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on people's minds," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Japan's top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi did nothing to ease the speculation. \par \par \uc2  He said current moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were short-term and authorities would take action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was only a matter of time before the euro hits its all-time high around 135.50 yen marked at its debut in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 134.29/34 yen compared with 134.40 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  The surging euro will provide European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers with one reason to leave interest rates steady at 2.50 percent at a meeting on Thursday as it squeezes inflationary pressure out of the economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030507dz5700bwk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
