\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar recovers vs yen on Snow,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2003\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - The dollar recovered from its latest nadir against the yen on Wednesday, supported by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's comments backing a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and worries over possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But sentiment towards the greenback remained bearish with dealers holding to their cautious views on the U.S. economic outlook, especially after the Federal Reserve cited a possible "unwelcome substantial fall in inflation" on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates steady at its policy meeting, saying the easing of global tensions associated with the war in Iraq had abated, but it cautioned that the timing and extent of an economic recovery remained uncertain. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed's decision to leave rates steady was well within market expectations but they've included a mention of a deflationary threat and that was pretty surprising," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  A further fall in rates would bode ill for the dollar as the euro has been drawing global funds, largely at the expense of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because of higher interest rates in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  In Asia, however, the dollar was helped by Snow's affirmation of a strong dollar policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters. \par \par \uc2  "We think a strong dollar is in the U.S. interest," Snow said in an interview on CNBC television. "The way to have a strong dollar and a dollar that is widely accepted as a good medium of exchange is to work on the fundamentals of the economy." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rebounded to 117.73/78 yen at 0306 GMT, from around 117.50 in late New York, and a one-month low around 117.29 yen hit in post-Asian trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1410/15 down from around $1.1440 in late U.S. business. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS \par \par \uc2  Tension in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been on the rise since the dollar fell beyond 118 yen because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted its first stealthy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the mid-117 yen level in January. \par \par \uc2  "We're at a level where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on people's minds," said Nomura Securities' Toyahara. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Japan's top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi helped the dollar's rise against the yen as well. \par \par \uc2  He said current moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were short-term and authorities would take action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  But despite the dollar's modest recovery, dealers expect such moves to be short-lived and that much action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be dominated by how well the euro performs. \par \par \uc2  The euro has been trading near four-year peaks against the dollar and the yen on a steady flow of funds into the higher yielding single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and many analysts say such trends will continue at least in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say it is only a matter of time before the euro hits its all-time high around 135.50 yen marked at its debut in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 134.37/40 yen compared with 134.40 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  For euro/dollar, the market is eyeing $1.15 as the next significant target. \par \par \uc2  The surging euro will provide European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers a reason to leave interest rates steady at 2.50 percent at a meeting on Thursday as it squeezes inflationary pressure out of the economy. \par \par \uc2  "I think the ECB will keep rates steady as we're seeing a steady flow of funds into the euro zone and higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are much in favour now," said a dealer at a major Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  But a growing number of dealers also acknowledge that the euro is heading towards dangerously strong levels and warn that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could reverse trends. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030507dz57006bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
