\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Edges Up Vs Yen On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2003\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar edged back up against the yen in Asia Wednesday, as growing fears of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  spooked players into covering dollar-short positions. \par \par \uc2  After sinking to a two-month low against the yen overnight, the U.S. unit got a lift from Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, who warned that the MOF is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap any excessive yen surge. \par \par \uc2  "We will take appropriate measures as needed" to curb excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, Mizoguchi said, suggesting the ministry is increasingly unhappy over the dollar's recent slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi's comments, following similar remarks Tuesday, added to fears the ministry may covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since early March to sell yen and put a floor under the weak dollar. \par \par \uc2  That threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some dollar demand toward the Tokyo retail fixing at 0100 GMT lifted the U.S. unit to around Y117.82 early in the session, but interbank-led profit-taking reduced those gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar may face downward pressure for the rest of the global session, given the underlying bearish sentiment over the U.S. economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with some traders expecting the dollar to test its overnight low of Y117.29. \par \par \uc2  Around 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.69, above Y117.54 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y118.58 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1412, lower than $1.1438 late Tuesday in New York. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $1.1285 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y134.29, down from Y134.44 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y133.78 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's MOF sold some Y2.4 trillion for dollars and euros on a number of occasions from the start of the year through early March to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, which was particularly fierce in the run-up to the U.S.-led war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  While the ministry has consistently denied it is seeking to manipulate the yen lower, Tokyo is widely known to oppose a sharp appreciation of the yen. \par \par \uc2  A strong yen makes Japanese exports less competitive in the foreign markets and adds to deflationary pressure at home. It also reduces the value of Japanese firms' overseas assets and earnings. \par \par \uc2  In the Asian session Wednesday, Japanese brokerage houses also bought Australian and Canadian dollars for yen, aiding the U.S. unit's rise against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Healthy demand among Japanese securities houses for Australian and Canadian dollars and the euro to purchase foreign securities for inclusion in high-yielding investment funds here have helped prop up the dollar in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting this trend, Daiwa Securities Group Inc. (J.DST or 8601) advertised investment trust funds containing Australian, Canadian and U.S. dollar-denominated bonds with high credit ratings in Wednesday's Nihon Keizai Shimbun. \par \par \uc2  While the amounts of those investment trust funds were not published in the newspaper, the Canadian bond investment trust fund was rumored to be as large as Y100 billion, a Tokyo dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6130, down from $1.6138 in New York but higher than $1.6069 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Hugh Lawson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030507dz570009m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
