\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro eases as traders square up ahead of Fed and ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2003\par 08:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 5 (Reuters) - The euro eased slightly in\par Asian trade on Monday as players booked some profits on its\par sharp rally ahead of policy-setting meetings of the Federal\par Reserve, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and Bank of England this week.\par     "The markets are looking at the Fed and ECB and before that\par they are trying to consolidate their positions," said a dealer\par at a European bank in Singapore.\par     Trading was thinned in Asia by a Japanese holiday, and\par Europe was expected to be affected by a holiday that will close\par London markets, and there was also caution over Japanese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. Federal Reserve meets on Tuesday and is expected\par to leave the fed funds rate unchanged at 1.25 percent. The\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meets on Thursday and was also expected\par to leave rates unchanged.\par  \par     In contrast, most economists polled by Reuters expect\par another rate cut by the Bank of England later this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     As traders paused ahead of the meetings and squared up some\par positions, the euro pulled back from last week's four-year\par highs of $1.1287 against the dollar and 133.78 on the yen.\par     That helped the yen move a notch higher against the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though it showed no inclination to head back to Thursday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-month high of 118.12 as dealers said its upside was limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The caution followed a Jiji Press report on Friday that\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would call for yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stimulus package expected to be announced this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par POLICY INACTION\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the lack of momentum on Monday was not only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to the holidays, but because the market had already priced\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the Fed's expected policy inaction on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Unless the Fed surprises, the market should stay in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range," said Lee Boon Keng, treasury markets strategist at DBS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A key factor would be the accompanying statement from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Federal Reserve. Comments suggesting a further U.S. easing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would support high yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the euro,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canadian dollar and Australian dollar - which all hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mutli-year highs on the dollar last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Naomi Fink, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the focus would shift back to U.S. fundamentals after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fed meeting. UBS Warburg expects no change in rates on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "While there may be some signs of recovery in the U.S.,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unless they are very strong what we are going to see is a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par return to the dollar bearish trend," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Data on Friday showed U.S. unemployment rising to 6.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent as the economy shed 48,000 jobs against forecasts of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5.9 percent jobless rate and 53,000 lost jobs. The market had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sold the dollar before the data, expecting poor news.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fink said a sustained U.S. stock market rise after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reporting season ended might help the dollar. But with U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates at historical lows, interest rate differentials were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to keep funds flowing towards the euro zone.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0632GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  2002 Cls\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.1210   1.1225   -0.13   +6.80   1.0496\par Dlr/yen              118.96   119.03   -0.06   +0.19   118.74\par Euro/yen             133.38   133.66   -0.21   +6.99   124.67\par Dlr/swiss            1.3476   1.3442   +0.25   -2.43   1.3812\par Stg/dlr              1.6025   1.6037   -0.07   -0.53   1.6110\par Dlr/can              1.4182   1.4183   -0.01   -9.80   1.5722\par Aus/dlr              0.6312   0.6300   +0.19  +12.53   0.5609\par Euro/swiss           1.5110   1.5092   +0.12   +4.24   1.4496\par Euro/stg             0.6992   0.6996   -0.06   +7.37   0.6512.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030505dz5500dqv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pic