\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro loses some steam, yen finds footing. \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2003\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 5 (Reuters) - The euro        lost some\par ground against the dollar and the yen  on Monday as\par traders locked in profits on its run to four-year highs as they\par readied for policy meetings of the major central banks this\par week.\par     The euro's slight pullback helped the yen        move a\par notch higher against the dollar in a market thinned by holidays\par in Tokyo and London, though dealers said the yen's upside was\par limited on fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities.\par     "The market will consolidate before taking fresh positions\par and that is what's happening," said a dealer at a Singapore\par bank, adding there was a reluctance to sell the dollar beyond\par the lows it hit on Friday.\par  \par     "People want to cut back some of their exposure to short\par dollar positions before moving ahead," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was also cautious after a Jiji Press report on\par Friday said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would call for yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par part of a stimulus package expected to be announced this week.\par     The report had accelerated the yen's move away from a\par one-month high of 118.12 per dollar hit on Thursday.\par     There was a lack of momentum at the start of the week as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players consolidated their positions ahead of U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-manufacturing ISM data due later in the day and meetings by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Federal Reserve and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/yen pulled back to around 133.40 yen from Friday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four-year high of 133.78, while the euro also edged down\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar towards $1.12, having hit a four-year high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of $1.1287 on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The U.S. Federal Reserve meets on Tuesday and is expected\par to  leave the fed funds rate unchanged at 1.25 percent. Double\par click         to see latest Fed poll. The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par meets on Thursday and was also expected to leave rates\par unchanged.\par     In contrast, most economists polled by Reuters expect\par another rate cut by the Bank of England later this week.\par     "The market has likely priced in the Fed's inaction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tomorrow. Hence, unless the Fed surprises, the market should\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stay in a range," said Lee Boon Keng, treasury markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategist at DBS Bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Apart from the euro, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Canadian dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Australian dollar also hit multi-year highs against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar last week, and dealers said the bearish sentiment on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was reinforced by Friday's grim U.S. employment data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. unemployment rose to 6.0 percent as the economy shed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 48,000 jobs, against forecasts of a 5.9 percent jobless rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 53,000 loss in jobs. The market had sold the dollar before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the data, expecting poor news.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0343GMT. All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  2002 Cls\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.1213   1.1225   -0.11   +6.83   1.0496\par Dlr/yen              118.98   119.03   -0.04   +0.20   118.74\par Euro/yen             133.45   133.66   -0.16   +7.04   124.67\par Dlr/swiss            1.3457   1.3442   +0.11   -2.57   1.3812\par Stg/dlr              1.6027   1.6037   -0.06   -0.52   1.6110\par Dlr/can              1.4193   1.4183   +0.07   -9.73   1.5722\par Aus/dlr              0.6307   0.6300   +0.11  +12.44   0.5609\par Euro/swiss           1.5092   1.5092   +0.00   +4.11   1.4496\par Euro/stg             0.6993   0.6996   -0.04   +7.39   0.6512.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030505dz55007pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
